From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: v8: ppc64 Assembler::mov wastes 4 instructions per immediate under a
 blocked trampoline pool

The guard that decides whether mov() may emit the short form reads

    canOptimize =
        !(relocatable ||
          (is_trampoline_pool_blocked() &&
           (!is_int16(value) ||
            !(CpuFeatures::IsSupported(PPC_10_PLUS) && is_int34(value)))));

Writing A for is_int16(value) and B for the PPC_10_PLUS && is_int34(value)
test, the inner term is (!A || !B).  On any processor below POWER10 B is false,
so !B is true, so the inner term is unconditionally true and the whole guard
collapses to

    canOptimize = !(relocatable || is_trampoline_pool_blocked());

Every non-relocatable immediate emitted inside a BlockTrampolinePoolScope then
takes bitwise_mov -- five instructions in a five-deep dependency chain -- even
for Operand(0), which li handles in one.

The body immediately below the guard admits exactly two single-instruction
cases, li for is_int16 and pli for is_int34 on POWER10, which is what the
trampoline-blocked arm was evidently meant to allow: while the pool is blocked,
only emit the short form when it is genuinely short.  That reading is
!(A || B), so the negation belongs outside the disjunction rather than
distributed over both halves.

Affected sites are the ones that block the pool deliberately: every deopt exit
(code-generator.cc blocks around them), GetLabelAddress and therefore Switch,
SwitchOnGeneratorState and SwitchOnSmiNoFeedback -- i.e. every generator and
async resume -- and AssembleArchTableSwitch.

Shortening a sequence inside a blocked region is safe for the trampoline
mechanism itself, which blocks to prevent a trampoline being inserted mid
sequence.  Callers that require a fixed-length, later-patchable sequence pass a
relocatable operand, and relocatable short-circuits the guard before the
trampoline test is reached, so those are unaffected.

Found while profiling Sparkplug output on POWER9: 141 relocatable and ~85
non-relocatable constant materialisations across 23 baseline functions, 4170
instructions total.  Upstreamable as-is; not ppc64le packaging specific.

--- a/v8/src/codegen/ppc/assembler-ppc.cc
+++ b/v8/src/codegen/ppc/assembler-ppc.cc
@@ -1338,8 +1338,8 @@
   canOptimize =
       !(relocatable ||
         (is_trampoline_pool_blocked() &&
-         (!is_int16(value) ||
-          !(CpuFeatures::IsSupported(PPC_10_PLUS) && is_int34(value)))));
+         !(is_int16(value) ||
+           (CpuFeatures::IsSupported(PPC_10_PLUS) && is_int34(value)))));
 
   if (!src.IsHeapNumberRequest() &&
       use_constant_pool_for_mov(dst, src, canOptimize)) {
